## Data Flow

```
.syncytium/  ──load──►  CanonicalContext  ──generate──►  GeneratedFile[]  ──write──►  bridge files
     ▲                                                                                        │
     └────────────────────  diff / prune / preserve user sections  ◄────────────────────────┘
```

`sync` writes every generated file, then prunes banner-tagged files that no rule
produces any more. `diff` compares content and reports `identical`, `modified`
(with a unified patch), `missing_on_disk`, and `unmanaged` (orphans).

## MCP Safety Model

Every advertised tool carries MCP `annotations` (`readOnlyHint`,
`destructiveHint`, `idempotentHint`, `openWorldHint`) from
`src/mcp/safety.ts`, and the server enforces a per-tool sliding-window call
budget in the same module. Destructive tools (`remove_rule`, `remove_decision`)
default to `dryRun: true`; an actual delete needs `dryRun: false` **and**
`confirm: true`. Before deleting, the engine archives the exact rule/ADR bytes
under `.syncytium/memory/trash/`, and `syncytium_restore` (plus
`listTrash`/`restoreFromTrash` in the library) can undo the operation.
`doctor` is read-only: it reports remediation strings but never executes them.

The contract is mechanical, not descriptive: every `inputSchema` is closed with
`additionalProperties: false` and documents each property, and every stable read
tool declares an `outputSchema` plus matching `structuredContent`. Mutation is
never hidden behind a read annotation — `validate` is read-only and the separate
`validate_fix` tool performs repairs.

## Discovery

`server.json` describes the npm package to `registry.modelcontextprotocol.io`,
and `mcpName` in `package.json` proves npm ownership. `.github/workflows/discoverability.yml`
regenerates `llms.txt` / `llms-full.txt`, validates the manifest, and publishes
it with GitHub OIDC; no credential is stored in the repository.

## Directory Layout

- `src/` — source code and adapters
- `tests/syncytium.test.ts` — 123 tests, build-first (`npm run build && tsc -p tsconfig.tests.json && node --test dist-tests/*.test.js`)
- `scripts/release.mjs` — verify → publish → CDN-poll → global install
- `.syncytium/` — single source of truth
  - `rules/` — canonical, stack-aware rules
  - `memory/decisions.md` — ADRs
  - `memory/handoff-history.json` — baton audit trail
  - `memory/lock.json` — machine-local lease (git-ignored)
  - `HANDOFF.md` — live agent state
